    s__DUMMY_HABIT(py_str("At %s a dummy is a habit rather than a need, so plan it rather than spring it: say \"dummies are for sleep now\" and take it away in the day first, then the nap one, then the night one, a step a week. A %s year old can be in on the plan, so pick the week together, and get the dummies out of the house rather than into a drawer. Expect a few rough nights and do not give it back mid-week: going back and forth is what makes it last."));
    s__DUMMY_OLDER(py_str("Past five a dummy is only worth acting on if it is pushing the teeth or the speech out of line, and that is a dentist's or a speech therapist's call rather than something to fix at home. Do not shame the child or turn it into a fight: say it is time, give the date, and most children drop it themselves once it is not a secret. If the teeth are moving or the speech is unclear, ask the dentist at the next check-up and say how often it is used."));
