    s__THE_NOT_WANTING(py_str("Then say that plainly and kindly, once, without a reason they have to argue with: \"I like you as a friend - I didn't want to leave you guessing.\" Keep it short, and be normal with them the next day, which is what makes it land as respect rather than a brush-off."));
    s__THE_ASKING_OUT(py_str("Name the thing and the day, then stop talking: \"I've liked talking to you this week - do you want to get a coffee on Saturday?\" A specific plan is far easier to say yes to than \"sometime\", and a plain message you thought about for a minute beats a clever one. If it is a no, take it as an answer and be normal the next day: that is what keeps the friendship and your dignity."));
    s__DATE_OUT(py_str("Pick something with a bit of movement, like a coffee and a walk or a gallery, so silences have scenery. Ask about what they would do with a free day and what they are into lately; questions about them beat clever lines every time."));
    s__DATE_AT_HOME(py_str("Stay in but give it a shape, or it turns into a night on the sofa with the telly: something you both put together at the table (tacos, a pizza each, a fondue), a playlist or a record on, and the phones in another room until the plates are cleared. It costs less than a bar and it gives you something to do with your hands while you talk."));
