    s__QUIET_CHILD_REPLY(py_str("Do not interview them: talk side by side, in the car or while doing something, and keep it to a couple of minutes. Ask about the small things and let the big one come later - a child who says nothing at seven often talks at ten. Say once that you are there and that you are not going to be cross, and then be that, because the second question is the one that closes the door. If it is weeks of silence, plus no friends, no eating or giving up things they loved, ask the GP or the school about CAMHS."));
