    s__QUIET_FRIEND_REPLY(py_str("Send one small, specific message - a photo with a line on it ('saw this and thought of you - how are you doing?'), or a question only they would know the answer to - and then leave it. {reason}One warm message is easy to answer where three is a job. If there is no reply, wait a month, then try once more and let it rest; a friendship that needs chasing that often is telling you something."));
    s__FRIEND_MOVED_REASON(py_str("A friend who has gone quiet after you moved is usually out of the loop rather than upset. "));
    s__FRIEND_QUIET_REASON(py_str("Most quiet stretches are a busy month or something they have not said, not a verdict on you. "));
    s__QUIET_GROWN_REPLY(py_str("Do not sit them down for a talk, which feels like an exam - a quiet adult usually dreads it rather than refusing it. Do something side by side, a drive or the washing up, say what you have noticed in one plain sentence, then ask one small question and let the answer be short. No advice until it is asked for, and say once that you are not going anywhere. Weeks of silence and a change in drink, sleep or food is a GP call; Samaritans is 116 123."));
